## Task 2: Mystery Shuffle Free-Play Mode

Add a "Mystery Shuffle" free-play mode to memory-quiz, reusing existing level/mode data — no new content system.

### FILE: core.js — extend

- Add `drawShuffleCards(save, count)` → returns `count` cards (default 6), each
  `{ cardId, levelId, modeId }`, randomly sampled WITHOUT replacement from the set
  of currently-unlocked levels (per `isLevelUnlocked`) crossed with all available
  modes. Reject/reroll duplicate levelId+modeId pairs within one draw.
- Cards are pure data — no separate progress tracking. Completing a card's game
  writes to the SAME `levels[id]` save entry as normal level play (stars, bestScore).
  Do not create a parallel "shuffle save."

### FILE: index.html + game.js — new `shuffle` screen

- Entry point: a button on the menu, alongside level-select and free-play, labeled
  e.g. "Mystery Mix".
- On entry, call `drawShuffleCards(save, 6)` once and hold that set in memory for
  the session (re-drawing only when the player returns to the menu and re-enters).
- Render `count` face-down cards (no info visible: not even locked/unlocked state —
  they're already guaranteed unlocked by the draw).
- Tap a face-down card → flip it to show `levelId` (grid size/tier icon) + `modeId`
  (icon/label) + that level's current best stars if any. Flipping is non-destructive:
  the card stays revealed permanently for the rest of this shuffle session, whether
  or not the player then plays it.
- Once a card is revealed, it shows a "Play" affordance. Tapping Play starts that
  level+mode combo exactly as level-select would.
- Revealing one card never hides or removes any other card — the player can flip
  as many as they want before deciding, and can flip more after playing one.
- After a run ends (win or lose), return to the shuffle screen with that card now
  showing the updated star/best result, all other cards' revealed/hidden state
  untouched.
- No "cards remaining" pressure mechanic and no timer — this mode is exploratory,
  not a limited-attempts challenge. ("Limited number" = the draw size, not a
  play-count budget.)

### Edge Cases

- Fewer than `count` unlocked level×mode combos exist (early game) → draw as many
  as are available, no error, no placeholder cards.
- Player unlocks a new level mid-shuffle-session → do not inject it into the
  current draw; it becomes eligible on the next shuffle entry.

### Testing (extend §8 suite)

- `drawShuffleCards`: no duplicate levelId+modeId pairs in one draw; only draws
  from unlocked levels; respects `count` when fewer combos exist than requested.